<!-- @after 9. Further Reading :: recap -->
### Say these in the interview

- **Agree scope first:** 3-5 functional requirements, 3-4 non-functional ones, and an explicit out-of-scope list.
- **Ask the questions that change the architecture** (scale, real-time or eventual, offline, API floor, cross-platform), then state your assumptions.
- **Draw one diagram** and name the server components in a paragraph; the backend stays a black box.
- **Go deep on one feature** with one or two snippets for the hard part and a failure-mode table.
- **Show trade-offs as tables with a verdict,** and raise process death, OEM kills and testing without being asked.
- **Defend your cuts with confidence:** "Out of scope here because…".
